{"effort": "high", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "recorded_at": "2026-10-29T04:16:54Z", "response": {"container": null, "content": [{"thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"caller": {"type": "direct"}, "id": "toolu_01XFQLa3dUPser4x7XvUcVNr", "input": {"claims": [{"citations": ["E-004442"], "quotes": [{"event_id": "E-004442", "field": "process.command_line", "text": "HarborBackup.exe --job nightly"}, {"event_id": "E-004442", "field": "process.parent.name", "text": "services.exe"}], "text": "HarborBackup.exe started as svc-backup, launched by services.exe, with a command line for a nightly job. This is consistent with a scheduled service. There were no child processes and no other suspicious activity in the 20 minutes around it."}, {"citations": ["E-004443"], "quotes": [{"event_id": "E-004443", "field": "dns.question.name", "text": "vault.offsite-backup.example"}, {"event_id": "E-004443", "field": "destination.ip", "text": "198.51.100.140"}], "text": "Five seconds after the process started, it made an HTTPS connection to an external host, vault.offsite-backup.example (198.51.100.140), which triggered the large-upload rule. The event has no byte count, so the size cannot be verified. The destination's legitimacy cannot be confirmed from the data."}, {"citations": ["E-004442", "E-004443"], "quotes": [], "text": "There is no baseline. WS-02 has no earlier HarborBackup.exe runs and no earlier lookups of the offsite-backup domain in the prior 24 hours. The only svc-backup activity on 2026-03-03 is this pair of events. It is therefore unclear whether this is a routine job or a first-time exfiltration-like transfer."}], "confidence": "low", "injection_reports": [], "recommended_actions": [{"action": "open_ticket", "citations": ["E-004442", "E-004443"], "id": "ACT-001", "reason": "Ask the client to confirm that HarborBackup.exe, the svc-backup account and the offsite vault vault.offsite-backup.example (198.51.100.140) are authorized, and that a nightly backup from WS-02 at about 13:16 UTC is expected. Escalate to block_ip or isolate_host if they deny it.", "target": "WS-02"}], "summary": "The alert looks like a scheduled backup. HarborBackup.exe ran as svc-backup under services.exe with \"--job nightly\" and uploaded over 443 to vault.offsite-backup.example (198.51.100.140). I found no malicious indicators, but I also found no baseline: no earlier runs of this process, no earlier traffic to that domain, and no upload size in the data. Someone needs to ask the client whether this backup product and offsite vault are authorized, and whether WS-02 should run backups at this time.", "verdict": "needs_human"}, "name": "submit_verdict", "type": "tool_use"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CgVt7SQ2Vtk7CPeaw8vUE", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 570}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 570, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5527, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1107, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 104}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "source": "live", "tool_results": [], "turn": 4}
